      {
        "id": 117080,
        "name": "dpt",
        "username": "dpt",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/{size}/1922_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-09-07T03:35:11.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Zondebok\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/z/e480ec/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Zondebok:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I get that this is not a competitive game, but it seems like one should be able to figure out what do to in a given situation by following the rules of the game. &nbsp;It seems like this snapshotting is not covered in the rules, but someone, somewhere has made an official ruling about it. &nbsp;I am fine either way, I just like to know all of the mechanics/rules and how to apply them :)&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I'm surprised no one answered this sooner: The basic answer is that there is never any \"snapshotting\", and all modifiers are always re-evaluated. There are definitely sticky situations, but they have to do in what order you evaluate various modifiers.</p>",
