      {
        "id": 117081,
        "name": "Sefirit",
        "username": "Sefirit",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/e68b1a/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-09-08T18:51:30.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I can't think of any off the top of my head honestly, but this game can be so situational at times that weird fringe cases can, and do, come up.OH! And Welcome to the forums!!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Doesn't Scholar have a couple of cards that might apply?&nbsp; Like do X damage where X is the number of non-hero targets out.&nbsp; I think the question is, on a card like that if there are six targets out when you start, but you kill some along the way does X stay six or does it decrease.&nbsp; I believe it stays six, but I'm not basing that off of anything.</p>",
        "post_number": 24,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:49:40.421Z",
