      {
        "id": 117082,
        "name": "Sonvar",
        "username": "Powerhound_2000",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/{size}/1859_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-09-08T19:04:24.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The Scholar's cards wouldn't have to do a recheck for X because of how they work. &nbsp; The one I believe you are thinking of is Grace Under Fire. &nbsp; It deals X damage to one target where X is the number of non hero targets in play. &nbsp;He would only need to check once before dealing the damage. &nbsp;He has two other cards with an X value to calculate from \"Get Out of the Way\" and Know when to turn Loose. &nbsp; The first heals him X for every target he damaged and the second is based on how many cards he discarded. &nbsp; So for all of his cards with X on it there should only be a need to calculate once. &nbsp;</p>",
