      {
        "id": 117090,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-09-10T15:54:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Matchstickman\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/48/1880_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Matchstickman:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If people are concurring there's no \"snapshotting\", that's (inadvertenly) how people are saying Checmical Explosion works.Far be it for me to disagree with the masses.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Chemical explosion still \"snapshot\" (meaning a fixed number independent of future game states). It's X is dependant upon how many Vats it destroys in its destruction sequence, and it only destroys Vats once, so any future game state won't be able to change it in the first place (unless more vats get played/destroyed during the destruction sequence obviously).&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 33,
